{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119634","id":3724397933,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7d_c1t","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119634","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119634.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119634.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119634","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119634/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119634/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119634/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/fcc194c585765d70112a77098544dce6b491012c","number":119634,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Android: Fix infinite recursion in proxy equals handler","user":{"login":"shiena","id":1295639,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyOTU2Mzk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1295639?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena","html_url":"https://github.com/shiena","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shiena/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Kotlin's `==` on the proxy compiles to `proxy.equals(args[0])`, which the JDK proxy dispatches back through the InvocationHandler, hitting the same branch and recursing into StackOverflowError. Use `===` for reference equality, matching the default Object#equals behavior.\r\n\r\nThis PR switches both branches from `==` to `===`. Reference equality matches the default `Object#equals` behavior, and is consistent with the identity-based `hashCode` the handler already returns (`godotCallable.hashCode()` and `godotObjectID`).\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n\r\nUse of AI must be disclosed and should include a description of how it was used.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #119632\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nVerified on a physical Android device using the MRP attached to #119632. Before the fix the MRP labels itself `BUG REPRODUCED` (`result=0`, exception holds `StackOverflowError`); after the fix it labels itself `FIX APPLIED` (`result=1`, no pending exception).\r\n\r\n#119622 fixes a similar slip in the adjacent `hashCode` branch of the same file (a `Long` returned where `Int` is required, causing `ClassCastException`). Independent of this PR.\r\n\r\n### AI disclosure\r\n\r\nClaude helped me dig into the bug, put together the MRP, and grep the rest of the engine for the same `==`/`===` mistake. Nothing else turned up. I wrote the actual fix, ran the MRP on a real Android device to confirm, and edited Claude's drafts before posting them.\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nProvide additional information and explanation of your PR, including areas that you are uncertain of or require special attention from reviewers. For examples, please read our pull request guidelines: https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/pull_requests/pull_request_guidelines.html#explain-your-contribution